@startuml
title AsyncSharedState — waiter registration / completion race
<style>
document {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BoxPadding 10
  ParticipantPadding 10
}
title {
  FontSize 16
  FontColor #111111
}
</style>

participant "Awaiting coroutine" as Awaiter
participant "AsyncSharedState<T>" as State
participant "Completing task" as Producer
participant "Selected executor" as Executor
participant "Dispatcher" as Dispatcher

note over State
  States: Pending, Suspended, Signaled.
  Result data is written before signalReady().
end note

alt Completion wins before waiter registration
  Producer -> State : write result
  Producer -> State : CAS Pending -> Signaled
  Awaiter -> State : await_ready() / inspect state
  State --> Awaiter : Signaled; do not suspend
  Awaiter -> Awaiter : consume result
else Waiter registration wins
  Awaiter -> State : store coroutine handle + executor
  Awaiter -> State : CAS Pending -> Suspended
  State --> Awaiter : registration succeeded
  Awaiter -> Dispatcher : transfer control to dispatcher
  ... task completes later ...
  Producer -> State : write result
  Producer -> State : CAS Suspended -> Signaled
  State -> Executor : execute(waiter handle)
  alt Scheduling succeeds
    Executor -> Dispatcher : enqueue waiter
    Dispatcher -> Awaiter : resume
  else Scheduling fails
    State -> Awaiter : resume inline fallback
  end
  Awaiter -> State : await_resume() / consume result
else Completion races registration
  par Awaiter attempts registration
    Awaiter -> State : CAS Pending -> Suspended
  else Producer attempts completion
    Producer -> State : write result; CAS Pending -> Signaled
  end
  note over Awaiter,Producer
    Only one Pending transition wins.
    If registration loses, await_suspend returns the
    awaiting coroutine handle for inline continuation.
    If completion observes Suspended, it schedules
    the stored waiter (or uses the inline fallback).
  end note
end

note over Awaiter,Producer
  Awaiting is single-consumer. Repeated/invalid consumer claims
  are contract violations and terminate; cancellation is a separate flag.
end note
@enduml
